{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["You drink the coffee and turn the cup upside down. The reader predicts the future, deciphering various patterns formed inside the cup.","Tasseomancy"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This is a deck of 78 cards with pictures and inscriptions on them. They are divided into several suits and the person extracts cards that the reader interprets.","Tarot"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This method of divination uses air and water. The person covers their head with a cloth, fill a vase with water and expose it to the air. They whisper a wish over the vase. If bubbles show on the water surface, this is considered a positive sign and the wish will probably come true.","Eromancy"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This method includes hexagrams which consist of six lines either solid or broken. Solid lines are considered strong and active, and broken lines stand for weak and acquiescent. These lines define the meaning of the hexagrams. Each hexagram has a different meaning. You determine your own hexagram by tossing 3 coins 3 times.","I Ching"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This method of divination uses a set of 24 alphabet letters that are usually carved on small tiles, so that the person could extract one of all 24 and to interpret its meaning. They were also carved and drawn building walls for protection.","Runes"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This is the careful screening of your palm, its shapes and lines in order to guess some events from the past and see events in the future.","Palmistry"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This method uses climate conditions to predict the future. It was considered that climate is the attitude of gods towards men, and that each atmospheric event had its own meaning.","Aeromancy"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This method uses books for predicting ones future. The person should take a book, open to a random page and read a passage. Then he should interpret it.","Bibliomancy"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This way of divination uses onion sprouts. First a ritual is held in order to state what the divination is about. Then the onion sprouts are put on an altar. It is thought that onion sprouts can tell you about friends and relatives who are far away, give love advice and answer yes or no questions about the future.","Cromniomancy"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["This method uses birds to predict the future. The divinator scatters grains and then he carefully observes the way the birds peck at the grain.","Alectryomancy"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["In ancient times people thought that illnesses were caused by demons, possessing the soul of a person. So they cured those illnesses with exorcism. Exorcism is derived from the Greek word exorkizein. What does this word mean?","To bind by oath"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Ancient Babylonian priests were one of the first exorcists. They meant to destroy the evil spirit, possessing the victim, by performing this ritual.","They destroyed a wax or clay image of a demon."],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Exorcism is not popular among religions nowadays.","False"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Jesus Christ is considered to be an exorcist. One of the legends tells of Jesus casting out multiple demons from a madman. The spirits then entered the bodies of some animals. What kind of animals were they?","Pigs"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Jesus Christ gave the power to exorcise demons to his disciples.","True"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["In Judaism the evil spirit that possesses the soul of its victim is called dybbuk. It is exorcised through this part of the body.","Small toe"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["The exorcist must feel as free of sin as possible. Why?","So demons cannot easily possess the exorcist"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Exorcism is related to ASC. What does ASC stand for?","Altered State Of Consciousness"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["During Christian exorcism, the victim is to hold a crucifix and the exorcist is encouraged to use holy water and relics. These two other objects should also be present.","Salt and Wine"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Although all exorcisms proceed differently, some stages are common. There are five common stages - The Presence, Break-point, The Voice, The Clash and this.","Expulsion"],"tags_json":"[\"trivia\",\"religion-faith\",\"source:open-trivia-qa\",\"license:cc-by-sa-4.0\"]"}
